  "claim": "The Antwerp-born writer of the song that was on the B-side of \"That's Me\" by pop group ABBA, was born on 16 December 1946. He also wrote and performed \"She's My Kind of Girl\".",
  "evidencia": "Page: Money, Money, Money. Sentence: \"Money, Money, Money\" is a song recorded by Swedish pop group ABBA, written by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus.\nPage: Benny Andersson. Sentence: Göran Bror Benny Andersson (] ; born 16 December 1946) is a Swedish musician, composer, member of the Swedish music group ABBA (1972–1982), and co-composer of the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\nPage: That's Me. Sentence: It was released as a single in Japan the following year (with \"Money, Money, Money\" as the B-side) to promote the band's \"Arrival\" album, and reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.\nPage: She's My Kind of Girl. Sentence: \"She's My Kind of Girl\" is a song written and performed by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus, who were later famous as members of ABBA.",
