        "original_id": "6a183383-cf30-5a4c-8f39-691534508970",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Organizations: ABBA\n- Songs: \"Money, Money, Money\", \"That's Me\", \"She's My Kind of Girl\"\n- Albums: \"Arrival\"\n- Musicals: \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n- Places: Japan\n\nFacts:\n- Benny Andersson was born on 16 December 1946 and is a Swedish musician and composer.\n- Benny Andersson was a member of ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Benny Andersson co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".\n- The song \"Money, Money, Money\" was recorded by ABBA and written by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus.\n- The song \"She's My Kind of Girl\" was written and performed by Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus before they became famous as members of ABBA.\n- In the year after \"Arrival\" was released, \"That's Me\" was issued as a single in Japan with \"Money, Money, Money\" as its B-side to promote the album \"Arrival\".\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
